<section id="Sx2.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Materials and Methods</h3>

</section>
<section id="Sx2.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Linear Velocity Feedback Delay Mitigation</h3>

<div id="Sx2.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We counteract the linear velocity delay experienced by the non-EKF-based platforms by overlaying a simple accelerometer integral that is grounded through an exponential decay. This can also be interpreted as a convolution of the accelerometer data with an Infinite Impulse Response (IIR) filter. Before the convolution, the gravity is subtracted by applying the current orientation estimate to the accelerometer data.</p>
<table id="Sx2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx2.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{a}_{g}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{a}_{g}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{R}^{T}(t)\mathbf{a}(t)-\mathbf{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐠</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{R}^{T}(t)\mathbf{a}(t)-\mathbf{g}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{v}_{a}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{v}_{a}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\mathbf{a}_{g}(\tau)e^{-\frac{t-\tau}{T}}d\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{t}\mathbf{a}_{g}(\tau)e^{-\frac{t-\tau}{T}}d\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We use the following discrete approximation to implement the filter:</p>
<table id="Sx2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx2.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=e^{\frac{\Delta t}{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=e^{\frac{\Delta t}{T}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{v}_{a}^{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{v}_{a}^{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha\mathbf{v}_{a}^{t-1}+\mathbf{a}_{g}^{t}\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha\mathbf{v}_{a}^{t-1}+\mathbf{a}_{g}^{t}\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We find that this mitigation significantly reduces the z-axis oscillations on the non-EKF-based platforms.</p>
</div>
<section id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Sampling Quadrotors</h4>

<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We establish a physically plausible posterior distribution over quadrotors through the following relations:</p>
<table id="Sx2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx2.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{\mathrm{t2w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t2w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{\mathrm{t2w}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(1.5,5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(1.5,5)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m_{\mathrm{min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m_{\mathrm{min}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0.02,\quad m_{\mathrm{max}}=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.02,\quad m_{\mathrm{max}}=5</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=s^{3},\quad s\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(\sqrt[3]{m_{\mathrm{min}}},\sqrt[3]{m_{\mathrm{max}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mroot><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mn>3</mn></mroot><mo>,</mo><mroot><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mn>3</mn></mroot><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=s^{3},\quad s\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(\sqrt[3]{m_{\mathrm{min}}},\sqrt[3]{m_{\mathrm{max}}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(\omega_{m_{i}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(\omega_{m_{i}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=c_{f_{0}}+c_{f_{1}}\omega_{m_{i}}+c_{f_{2}}\omega_{m_{i}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=c_{f_{0}}+c_{f_{1}}\omega_{m_{i}}+c_{f_{2}}\omega_{m_{i}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\omega_{m_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\omega_{m_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in[0,1],\;\sum_{i}C_{f_{i}}=1,\;C_{f_{0}}=0.038,\;C_{f_{1}}=0.154,\;C_{f_{2}}=0.987" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.038</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.154</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.447em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.987</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in[0,1],\;\sum_{i}C_{f_{i}}=1,\;C_{f_{0}}=0.038,\;C_{f_{1}}=0.154,\;C_{f_{2}}=0.987</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=r_{\mathrm{t2w}}\cdot 9.81\cdot m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t2w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>9.81</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=r_{\mathrm{t2w}}\cdot 9.81\cdot m</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{f_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{f_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C_{f_{i}}\frac{T}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C_{f_{i}}\frac{T}{4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The idea is to first sample the thrust-to-weight ratio <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{t2w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t2w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{t2w}}</annotation></semantics></math> and mass <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> to create the thrust curve. The thrust curve consists of the coefficients <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f_{0}},C_{f_{1}},C_{f_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f_{0}},C_{f_{1}},C_{f_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> for the constant, linear and quadratic term respectively. To relate the thrust-to-weight ratio to the thrust curve we require the mass. To sample the mass we need to consider that it grows cubically with the size (arm length, assuming constant density). If we were to uniformly sample the mass, we would disproportionately bias the distribution towards large quadrotors. Instead, we pose that quadrotors are rather uniformly distributed in size so we uniformly sample a scale <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> that we map back cubically into the desired mass range <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\in[m_{\mathrm{min}},m_{\mathrm{max}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\in[m_{\mathrm{min}},m_{\mathrm{max}}]</annotation></semantics></math> to get a realistic distribution over masses. Note that w.l.o.g., we normalize the motor effort setpoints <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{m_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{m_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the baseline thrust curve coefficients <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This allows us to simply scale the baseline thrust curve shape (taken from the Crazyflie <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>) to reflect the sampled thrust-to-weight ratio. Note: The baseline thrust curve coefficients <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{f_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{f_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> are capitalized while the coefficients <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{f_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{f_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> of the sampled thrust curve <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> are lower-case.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Due to different design considerations, the mass-size ratio <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sqrt[3]{m}}{l_{\mathrm{arm}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mroot><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></mroot><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>arm</mi></msub></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sqrt[3]{m}}{l_{\mathrm{arm}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is not always constant so we establish the mass-size ratio of the Crazyflie <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{ms}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{ms}</annotation></semantics></math> as the base value and sample variations around that.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Sx2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx2.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{ms}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{ms}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt[3]{m_{\text{crazyflie}}}}{l_{\mathrm{arm},\mathrm{crazyflie}}}\approx 7.90" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mroot><msub><mi>m</mi><mtext>crazyflie</mtext></msub><mn>3</mn></mroot><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi>arm</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>crazyflie</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≈</mo><mn>7.90</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt[3]{m_{\text{crazyflie}}}}{l_{\mathrm{arm},\mathrm{crazyflie}}}\approx 7.90</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}(-0.1,0.1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathcal{N}(-0.1,0.1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s_{ms}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s_{ms}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{1-u}&amp;\text{if }u&lt;0\\
1+u&amp;\text{if }u\geq 0\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{1-u}&amp;\text{if }u&lt;0\\
1+u&amp;\text{if }u\geq 0\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{ms}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{ms}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt[3]{m}}{l_{\mathrm{arm}}}\overset{!}{=}s_{ms}R_{ms}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mroot><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></mroot><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>arm</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">!</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt[3]{m}}{l_{\mathrm{arm}}}\overset{!}{=}s_{ms}R_{ms}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle l_{\mathrm{arm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>arm</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle l_{\mathrm{arm}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt[3]{m}}{s_{ms}R_{ms}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mroot><mi>m</mi><mn>3</mn></mroot><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt[3]{m}}{s_{ms}R_{ms}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We intended to use a reciprocal deviation <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{\mathrm{ms}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>ms</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{\mathrm{ms}}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 10\%</annotation></semantics></math> but accidentally used a normal instead of a uniform distribution. In a post-hoc analysis we find that the resulting distribution has a mean and standard deviation of <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 7.24\pm 0.66" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>7.24</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>0.66</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 7.24\pm 0.66</annotation></semantics></math>. This incidentally fits the empirical distribution of mass-size deviations of the quadrotors in Figure <a href="#S2.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 2.4 Deployment ‣ 2 Results ‣ RAPTOR: A Foundation Policy for Quadrotor Control" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> with a mean and standard deviation of <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 7.66\pm 1.93" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>7.66</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>1.93</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 7.66\pm 1.93</annotation></semantics></math> better than the intended distribution of just <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\%</annotation></semantics></math> uniform reciprocal deviations. For future works we advise to investigate directly sampling from a normal distribution with a wider standard deviation that is closer to the empirical standard deviation of the actual quadrotors.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The sampled mass-size ratio allows us to compute the arm length <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{\mathrm{arm}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>arm</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{\mathrm{arm}}</annotation></semantics></math> which, in combination with the assumption that the quadrotor is in a symmetric X configuration, defines the geometry.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we need to sample the inertia based on the previously sampled quantities:</p>
<table id="Sx2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{\mathrm{t2i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t2i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{\mathrm{t2i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(40,1200)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1200</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(40,1200)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=T\cdot\sqrt{2}\cdot l_{\mathrm{arm}}\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>arm</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=T\cdot\sqrt{2}\cdot l_{\mathrm{arm}}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{xx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{xx}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=J_{yy}=\frac{\tau}{r_{\mathrm{t2i}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t2i</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=J_{yy}=\frac{\tau}{r_{\mathrm{t2i}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{zz}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{zz}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{J_{xx}+J_{yy}}{2}\cdot 1.832" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1.832</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{J_{xx}+J_{yy}}{2}\cdot 1.832</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">For sampling the inertia, we introduce another ratio, the torque-to-inertia ratio <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathrm{t2i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t2i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathrm{t2i}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We collect quadrotor dynamics parameters from the literature and find a realistic randomization range to be between <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="40" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>40</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">40</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1200</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1200</annotation></semantics></math>. After sampling the torque-to-inertia ratio, we can use the previously sampled thrust-to-weight, mass and size (arm length) parameters to calculate the x and y inertia. To get the z inertia, we apply the rule of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, we can independently sample the moment constant as well as the motor delays because they do not correlate strongly with any of the other variables in our experience:</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Sx2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(0.005,0.05)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.005</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(0.005,0.05)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{m\uparrow}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{m\uparrow}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(0.03,0.1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.03</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(0.03,0.1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{m\downarrow}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{m\downarrow}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(0.03,0.3)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Uniform</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.03</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.3</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sim\mathrm{Uniform}(0.03,0.3)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Sampling Trajectories</h4>

<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During pre-training, the policies are Markovian and only consider the current observation (plus previous actions). This means that (in the absence of aerial drag-forces from linear velocity) trajectory tracking and position control appear identical to the policy because we can just feed the position and linear velocity error w.r.t. the trajectory as observations and achieve good trajectory tracking <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>. In the case of a stateful, non-Markovian policy as with the recurrent foundation policy, this is not the case anymore. If we add the dynamics of the trajectory itself to the dynamics of the quadrotor through the error-state observation, the trajectory of error-state observations does not appear like a quadrotor anymore.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A simple example would be a reference trajectory with a jump in linear velocity. From the perspective of a stateful policy that has only been trained on position control (no trajectory dynamics in the observation space) this abrupt change in linear velocity appears like a quadrotor with an unrealistically high thrust-to-weight ratio, unrealistically fast angular response and/or even a world with much larger than <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> G gravity. The latter happens if e.g., the velocity step is downwards in z and the quadrotor is not upside down or if the action inputs have been low/zero.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To counter-act this, we train the expert and student policies using a simple probabilistic mixture model of trajectories. With <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50\%</annotation></semantics></math> probability the task is just tracking the null-trajectory (position control, going back to the origin from any initial state). In the other <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50\%</annotation></semantics></math> the task is to track randomly sampled trajectories.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We would like to cover a wide variety of possible reference trajectories. Trajectories are vector-valued functions of time so we need to design a broad distribution over functions. Here we take inspiration from the Gaussian Process (GP) community, which has been concerned with designing prior distributions over functions since its inception. Additionally, we require the sampling of reference trajectories to not slow down the simulation too much. Hence we choose to sample the reference trajectories from a second-order Langevin process. A second-order Langevin process corresponds to a GP with a certain structure in the kernel (depending on the parameters of the Langevin process) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">54</a>, <a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">55</a>]</cite> but we can easily sample it incrementally while simulating the quadrotor dynamics.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Based on the results described in Section <a href="#S2.SS4.SSS1" title="2.4.1 Trajectory Tracking ‣ 2.4 Deployment ‣ 2 Results ‣ RAPTOR: A Foundation Policy for Quadrotor Control" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4.1</span></a>, we find that this approach works well for moderately agile trajectory tracking and even generalizes from second-order Langevin random walks to cyclical Lissajous trajectories. But we acknowledge that, while the second-order Langevin process covers the space of smooth functions relatively well, many trajectories with real-world use-cases like e.g., step-functions/responses are not covered or exponentially unlikely (e.g., cyclical trajectories).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Meta-Imitation Learning Objective</h4>

<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We do not perform variational inference in a case-by-case basis but instead in an amortized fashion, where the inference itself is conducted by the recurrent neural network policy at test time. This amortization makes the inference very compute efficient and allows us to deploy the foundation policy onto even the tiniest microcontrollers while meeting real-time constraints at high frequencies.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For tractability of the KL divergence we assume the action distributions are parameterized Gaussians:</p>
<table id="Sx2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\mid\mathbf{s}_{t},\boldsymbol{\Xi})\approx\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚵</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≈</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\mid\mathbf{s}_{t},\boldsymbol{\Xi})\approx\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*};\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}(\mathbf{s}_{t},\boldsymbol{\Xi}),\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚵</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*};\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}(\mathbf{s}_{t},\boldsymbol{\Xi}),\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}(\mathbf{s}_{t},\boldsymbol{\Xi}):=\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚵</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">:=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}(\mathbf{s}_{t},\boldsymbol{\Xi}):=\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}_{\boldsymbol{\Xi}}(\mathbf{s}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>𝚵</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}_{\boldsymbol{\Xi}}(\mathbf{s}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{\pi}\mid\mathbf{o}_{0},\ldots,\mathbf{o}_{t},\mathbf{a}_{0},\ldots,\mathbf{a}_{t-1})\approx\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≈</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{\pi}\mid\mathbf{o}_{0},\ldots,\mathbf{o}_{t},\mathbf{a}_{0},\ldots,\mathbf{a}_{t-1})\approx\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{\pi};\boldsymbol{\pi}(\mathbf{o}_{0},\ldots," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo>;</mo><mrow><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{\pi};\boldsymbol{\pi}(\mathbf{o}_{0},\ldots,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{o}_{t},\mathbf{a}_{0},\ldots,\mathbf{a}_{t-1}),\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{o}_{t},\mathbf{a}_{0},\ldots,\mathbf{a}_{t-1}),\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E31.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{\pi};\boldsymbol{\pi}(\mathbf{o}_{0:t},\mathbf{a}_{0:t-1}),\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo>;</mo><mi>𝝅</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{\pi};\boldsymbol{\pi}(\mathbf{o}_{0:t},\mathbf{a}_{0:t-1}),\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Where <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}_{\boldsymbol{\Xi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝝅</mi><mi>𝚵</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}_{\boldsymbol{\Xi}}</annotation></semantics></math> is one of the <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1000</annotation></semantics></math> teacher policies trained for the particular quadrotor/set of dynamics parameters <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Xi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚵</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Xi}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> is the student foundation policy.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We can see that the input shape of the foundation policy <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> is dependent on the number of previous steps in the episode. Due to the sequential nature of the inputs, we choose a recurrent neural network architecture for three main reasons:</p>
<ul id="Sx2.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="Sx2.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Computational Efficiency</span>: We require computational efficiency for direct deployment on compute-constrained microcontrollers. Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs) are <math id="Sx2.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> in the history length <math id="Sx2.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, each incremental step only requires a fixed amount of compute at inference time. In contrast, Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN) and attention are <math id="Sx2.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\log(N))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\log(N))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx2.I3.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(N)</annotation></semantics></math> for each step, respectively.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Context Window Extrapolation</span>: At inference time we would like the policy to fly for longer time than the context window used during training. During training the context is usually limited to not slow down the process too much. CNNs, by design, have a limited context window that cannot be extended. Similarly attention, being a set-to-set mapping, requires position embeddings which complicate context window extrapolation.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Sx2.I3.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="Sx2.I3.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.I3.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx2.I3.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Successful Use in Related Works</span>: E.g. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>]</cite> have used recurrent policies successfully.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We find that a surprisingly small (in terms of number of parameters and compute requirements) three-layer recurrent neural network is sufficient to express the desired behavior described in Section <a href="#S1" title="1 Introduction ‣ RAPTOR: A Foundation Policy for Quadrotor Control" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Figure <a href="#S4.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ 4 Materials and Methods ‣ RAPTOR: A Foundation Policy for Quadrotor Control" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>B shows the architecture which contains a dense input layer, Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU) layer and a dense output layer. The initialization of the recurrent state (value at step <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>) is all zeros and we feed back the previous output of the policy as an input. Due to the small hidden dimensions the foundation policy only has <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2084" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2084</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2084</annotation></semantics></math> parameters:</p>
<table id="Sx2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx2.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;P_{\text{input}}+P_{\text{GRU}}+P_{\text{output}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>GRU</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>output</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;P_{\text{input}}+P_{\text{GRU}}+P_{\text{output}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{\text{input}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>input</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{\text{input}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E33.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;22\cdot 16+16=368" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn> 22</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>368</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;22\cdot 16+16=368</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{\text{GRU}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>GRU</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{\text{GRU}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;16\cdot 16\cdot 3\cdot 2+16\cdot 3\cdot 2+16=1648" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn> 16</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1648</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;16\cdot 16\cdot 3\cdot 2+16\cdot 3\cdot 2+16=1648</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P_{\text{output}}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>output</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P_{\text{output}}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;16\cdot 4+4=68" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn> 16</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>68</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;16\cdot 4+4=68</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;2084" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn> 2084</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;2084</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We train the foundation policy using Meta-Imitation Learning where it acts as the student. During Meta-Imitation Learning, we want to adjust the students weights to minimize the KL divergence (also known as relative entropy) between the predicted optimal action distribution by the student and the optimal action distribution (approximated by the particular teacher for the current system dynamics):</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Sx2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx2.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\bigl(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\,\|\,\mathbf{a}_{t}^{\pi}\bigr)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\bigl(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\,\|\,\mathbf{a}_{t}^{\pi}\bigr)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E37.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\;\underset{\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\sim p(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\mid\mathbf{s}_{t},\boldsymbol{\Xi})}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\log\frac{p(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\mid\mathbf{s}_{t},\boldsymbol{\Xi})}{p(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{\pi}=\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\mid\mathbf{o}_{0:t},\mathbf{a}_{0:t-1})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝐚</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.700em">∼</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝐚</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.710em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝐬</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">𝚵</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚵</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝐨</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\underset{\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\sim p(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\mid\mathbf{s}_{t},\boldsymbol{\Xi})}{\mathbb{E}}\left[\log\frac{p(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\mid\mathbf{s}_{t},\boldsymbol{\Xi})}{p(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{\pi}=\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\mid\mathbf{o}_{0:t},\mathbf{a}_{0:t-1})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left[\ldots\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[\ldots\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;\log p(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\mid\mathbf{s}_{t},\boldsymbol{\Xi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚵</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\log p(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\mid\mathbf{s}_{t},\boldsymbol{\Xi})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\;-\log p(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{\pi}=\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\mid\mathbf{o}_{0:t},\mathbf{a}_{0:t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;-\log p(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{\pi}=\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\mid\mathbf{o}_{0:t},\mathbf{a}_{0:t-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Hence we want to find the log probabilities of the action distributions that we approximated as Gaussians before:</p>
<table id="Sx2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx2.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\mu},\boldsymbol{\Sigma})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\mu},\boldsymbol{\Sigma})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E41.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\;(2\pi)^{-k/2}\det(\boldsymbol{\Sigma})^{-1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;(2\pi)^{-k/2}\det(\boldsymbol{\Sigma})^{-1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;\cdot\exp\!\left(-\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})^{\mathsf{T}}\boldsymbol{\Sigma}^{-1}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\cdot\exp\!\left(-\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})^{\mathsf{T}}\boldsymbol{\Sigma}^{-1}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\mu},\mathbf{I})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\mu},\mathbf{I})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;C\cdot\exp\!\left(-\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})^{\mathsf{T}}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;C\cdot\exp\!\left(-\frac{1}{2}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})^{\mathsf{T}}(\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E44.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;C\cdot\exp\!\left(-\frac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu}\|_{2}^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;C\cdot\exp\!\left(-\frac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{x}-\boldsymbol{\mu}\|_{2}^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Since we are aiming at quadrotors, both, the numerator and denominator multivariate Gaussian are 4 dimensional and the constants cancel.</p>
<table id="Sx2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx2.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left[\ldots\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[\ldots\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;\log p(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\mid\mathbf{s}_{t},\boldsymbol{\Xi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚵</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\log p(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\mid\mathbf{s}_{t},\boldsymbol{\Xi})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\;-\log p(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{\pi}=\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\mid\mathbf{o}_{0:t},\mathbf{a}_{0:t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;-\log p(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{\pi}=\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\mid\mathbf{o}_{0:t},\mathbf{a}_{0:t-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T}:=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T}:=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E47.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}(\mathbf{s}_{t},\boldsymbol{\Xi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚵</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}(\mathbf{s}_{t},\boldsymbol{\Xi})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\mu}_{S}:=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\mu}_{S}:=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E48.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\pi}(\mathbf{o}_{0:t},\mathbf{a}_{0:t-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝅</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\boldsymbol{\pi}(\mathbf{o}_{0:t},\mathbf{a}_{0:t-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left[\ldots\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[\ldots\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;\log C-\frac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{a}^{*}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\log C-\frac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{a}^{*}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;-\log C+\frac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{a}^{*}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{S}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;-\log C+\frac{1}{2}\|\mathbf{a}^{*}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{S}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p6.3" class="ltx_p">We can split the second squared norm:</p>
<table id="Sx2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathbf{a}^{*}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{S}\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathbf{a}^{*}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{S}\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;\|(\mathbf{a}^{*}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T})+\left(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{S}\right)\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\|(\mathbf{a}^{*}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T})+\left(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{S}\right)\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;\|(\mathbf{a}^{*}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T})\|_{2}^{2}+2(\mathbf{a}^{*}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T})^{\mathsf{T}}(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{S})+\|(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{S})\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\|(\mathbf{a}^{*}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T})\|_{2}^{2}+2(\mathbf{a}^{*}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T})^{\mathsf{T}}(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{S})+\|(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{S})\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p6.4" class="ltx_p">Plugging back into Eq. <a href="#Sx2.E44" title="In Meta-Imitation Learning Objective ‣ Linear Velocity Feedback Delay Mitigation ‣ Acknowledgments ‣ RAPTOR: A Foundation Policy for Quadrotor Control" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S44</span></a>:</p>
<table id="Sx2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx2.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left[\ldots\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[\ldots\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;(\mathbf{a}^{*}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T})^{\mathsf{T}}(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{S})+\frac{1}{2}\|(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{S})\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;(\mathbf{a}^{*}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T})^{\mathsf{T}}(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{S})+\frac{1}{2}\|(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{S})\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p6.5" class="ltx_p">We remember that we take the expectation over <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left[\ldots\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left[\ldots\right]</annotation></semantics></math> in Eq. <a href="#Sx2.E37" title="In Meta-Imitation Learning Objective ‣ Linear Velocity Feedback Delay Mitigation ‣ Acknowledgments ‣ RAPTOR: A Foundation Policy for Quadrotor Control" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">S37</span></a> and that we assume that the teacher is an unbiased estimator for the optimal action (<math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbf{a}^{*}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T}\right]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\mathbf{a}^{*}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T}\right]=0</annotation></semantics></math>):</p>
<table id="Sx2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx2.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\bigl(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\,\|\,\mathbf{a}_{t}^{\pi}\bigr)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐚</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\bigl(\mathbf{a}_{t}^{*}\,\|\,\mathbf{a}_{t}^{\pi}\bigr)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\;\frac{1}{2}\|(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{S})\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\frac{1}{2}\|(\boldsymbol{\mu}_{T}-\boldsymbol{\mu}_{S})\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx2.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx2.E53.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\;\frac{1}{2}\|(\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}(\mathbf{s}_{t},\boldsymbol{\Xi})-\boldsymbol{\pi}(\mathbf{o}_{0:t},\mathbf{a}_{0:t-1}))\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝝅</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚵</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝅</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐨</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\;\frac{1}{2}\|(\boldsymbol{\pi}^{*}(\mathbf{s}_{t},\boldsymbol{\Xi})-\boldsymbol{\pi}(\mathbf{o}_{0:t},\mathbf{a}_{0:t-1}))\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(S53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Hence, under the mild assumption of unit standard deviations, we can conduct the Meta-Imitation Learning in a principled manner by minimizing the relative differential entropy between the (approximated) optimal action distribution and the predicted optimal action distribution by the student. In practice, we implement this by using Eq. <a href="#Sx2.Ex5" title="Meta-Imitation Learning Objective ‣ Linear Velocity Feedback Delay Mitigation ‣ Acknowledgments ‣ RAPTOR: A Foundation Policy for Quadrotor Control" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Meta-Imitation Learning Objective</span></a>, which is identical to the Mean-Squared Error (MSE), as the loss function and by optimizing the student policy’s parameters <math id="Sx2.SSx2.SSSx3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> using gradient descent.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Sx2.F1" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.11481v1/sampling-quadrotors-graphical-model.svg" id="Sx2.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/168;" width="238" height="168"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Sx2.F1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Figure S1</span>: </span><span id="Sx2.F1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Probabilistic Graphical Model for Ancestral Sampling of Quadrotors</span></figcaption>
</figure>
